---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/seo';

// E-E-A-T / transparency page: how stories get made (including the AI-assisted
// drafting), sourcing standards, and the corrections policy. Linked from the
// footer. Static (repo, not Notion) so it ships with the site unconditionally.
const description =
  'How The Geo-Traveller is written and edited — sourcing standards, our use of AI-assisted drafting with human review, and how to request a correction.';
---

<Base title="Editorial policy" description={description}>
  <div class="policy">
    <h1 class="page-title">Editorial policy</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">How stories on {SITE.name} get researched, written and corrected.</p>

    <h2>Who's behind this site</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is written and edited by <a href="/about/">{SITE.author.name}</a> —
      a travel writer and photographer documenting India and beyond. It is an
      independent publication: nobody pays us to cover (or not cover) a
      destination, airline or restaurant.
    </p>

    <h2>How stories are made</h2>
    <p>
      We use AI tools as part of our writing workflow, and we'd rather say so
      plainly than bury it. Here is exactly how it works:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Research &amp; drafting.</strong> Story ideas come from primary
        sources — official announcements, news reports, search trends, and our
        own travel. Drafts may be prepared with the help of AI writing tools,
        always grounded in a real, cited source article.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Human review before publishing.</strong> Nothing is published
        automatically. Every draft sits in an editorial queue where it is
        reviewed, fact-checked against its sources, and edited by a human
        before it goes live.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sourcing.</strong> News stories link to the underlying source.
        Guides note when information (visa rules, fares, opening hours) was
        last verified — these things change, so always confirm with the
        official source before you book or travel.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Images.</strong> Photography is our own or sourced from
        licensed / freely-licensed providers (Unsplash, Pexels, Pixabay,
        Wikimedia Commons) with appropriate attribution.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Updates &amp; corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Guides are living documents: when the facts change, we update the guide
      in place and stamp it with an “Updated” date. If we get something wrong,
      we fix the article and note the correction rather than quietly rewriting
      history.
    </p>
    <p>
      Spotted an error? Tell us via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or
      email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.author.email}`}>{SITE.author.email}</a> —
      corrections are typically reviewed within a few days.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising &amp; affiliations</h2>
    <p>
      If a story ever contains sponsored content or affiliate links, it will be
      clearly disclosed in that story. Editorial decisions — what we cover and
      what we recommend — are never sold.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .policy p,
  .policy li {
    color: var(--fg-soft);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .policy li {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
